==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
From Germanic ''*ixwa-, *iwa-'', from {{proto|Indo-European|h₁éḱwos|horse|lang=ang}}.  Cognate with Old High German [[eha-]] (in personal names), Old Norse [[jór]].  The IE root is also the source of Latin [[equus]], Avestan ''aspa-'', Armenian {{term|էշ||donkey|tr=ēš|lang=hy}}, Tocharian A ''yuk'' B ''yakwe'', {{proto|Baltic|ečwā-|lang=}} (Lithuanian [[ašva|ašvà]]), Old Irish [[ech]] (Irish [[each]]).

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/eox/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
'''eoh''' ''m'' (plural {{unicode|'''[[eos|eōs]]'''}})

# {{poetic|lang=ang}} [[horse]], [[steed]]

===Etymology 2===
A variant of [[iw|īw]], representing a West Germanic variant ''*īhaz''; cognate with Old Saxon [[ich|īch]], Old High German [[igo|īgo]].

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/e:ox/|lang=ang}}

====Noun====
{{unicode|'''ēoh'''}} ''m''

# {{poetic|lang=ang}} [[yew]] tree
# the runic character '''[[ᛇ]]''' (/eo/ or /e:o/)

